Aim: 
To write a PL/SQL block that accepts a number from the user and checks whether it is even or odd.

Algorithm:
1. Start.
2. Accept a number from the user.
3. Check the remainder after division by 2.
4. Display whether the number is even or odd.
5. Stop.

Program:
SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;
DECLARE
    N NUMBER := &N;
BEGIN
    IF MOD(N, 2) = 0 THEN
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Number is Even');
    ELSE
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Number is Odd');
    END IF;
END;
/

Result: 
The program accepts a number and displays whether it is even or odd.
